connect-ip-go integration/ changes for interop/connect-ip/run.sh (docs/interop.md).
Applied with `git apply` on the pinned tag. The library, the docker-compose files and
the server are unchanged; so is the protocol behaviour of the client and the proxy
except for the address requests below.

1. client: with REQUEST_ADDRS (comma-separated prefixes, at least two), after the tunnel
   is up it requests them with Conn.RequestAddresses, reads the next address assignment
   (Conn.ReceiveAddressAssignment, 10 s) and requires the first request ID assigned with
   the requested prefix and the second rejected; it prints
   `address-request: ok ids=<a>,<b>` and runs TESTCASE, and exits non-zero otherwise.
   The stock client never sends an ADDRESS_REQUEST, so the correlation cell needs it.
2. proxy: answers every ADDRESS_REQUEST (Conn.ReceiveAddressRequest, AddressRequest.Respond)
   by the rule of h3wire's ip-proxy: ASSIGN_ADDR if the requested prefix is its host
   prefix or the all-zero address of its family, a rejection otherwise; ASSIGN_ADDR is
   added with request ID 0 when no entry got it, so the assignment stays the full list.
   The stock proxy assigns only unsolicited and leaves requests unanswered, though
   RFC 9484 section 4.7.2 says each Requested Address SHALL get one (rfc9484.txt line 658).

